From: ViKing <viking.yfy@qq.com>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 14:06:01 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: ath12k: select valid link for unspecified TX link

Group frames without a STA and an explicit link can select a deflink
storage slot which has been cleared after link removal. Use the first
active driver-backed link so broadcasts are not dropped on another link.

Adapted to the backports 7.2 ath12k shared MAC implementation from
perceival/openwrt-flint3 commit 2365932733ca8ec3b346621d9cec2eb3df3b2cf3.

Signed-off-by: ViKing <viking.yfy@qq.com>
---
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/mac.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/mac.c
@@ -9589,12 +9589,17 @@ u8 ath12k_mac_get_tx_link(struct ieee802
 	struct ieee80211_link_sta *link_sta;
 	struct ieee80211_bss_conf *bss_conf;
 	struct ath12k_sta *ahsta;
+	unsigned long links_map;
 
 	/* Use the link id passed or the default vif link */
 	if (!sta) {
 		if (link != IEEE80211_LINK_UNSPECIFIED)
 			return link;
 
+		links_map = vif->active_links & ahvif->links_map;
+		if (links_map)
+			return __ffs(links_map);
+
 		return ahvif->deflink.link_id;
 	}
 
